https://www.techrxiv.org/doi/pdf/10.36227/techrxiv.175760292.25429267/v1", "any_repository_has_fulltext": null}, "primary_location": {"id": "doi:10.36227/techrxiv.175760292.25429267/v1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.36227/techrxiv.175760292.25429267/v1", "is_oa": true, "landing_page_url": "https://doi.org/10.36227/techrxiv.175760292.25429267/v1", "pdf_url": "https://www.techrxiv.org/doi/pdf/10.36227/techrxiv.175760292.25429267/v1", "source": null, "license": "cc-by", "license_id": "https://openalex.org/licenses/cc-by", "version": "acceptedVersion", "is_accepted": true, "is_published": false, "raw_source_name": null, "raw_type": "posted-content"}, "abstract": "The proliferation of Large Language Model (LLM) agents has highlighted critical limitations in existing memory-augmented learning approaches, particularly for multi-agent coordination and high-stakes applications. While recent singleagent memory frameworks have shown promise, they lack theoretical rigor, formal convergence guarantees, and coordinated learning mechanisms required for financial services applications. This paper presents Multi-Agent Memento (MA-Memento), a theoretically grounded framework that fundamentally advances beyond existing memory-based approaches through: (1) formal Memory-Augmented Markov Decision Process (M-MDP) foundations with proven convergence guarantees, (2) novel multi-agent coordination mechanisms for distributed learning, (3) regulatory-compliant interpretability through transparent case-based reasoning, and (4) specialized architecture for high-stakes financial applications. Our comprehensive experimental evaluation across eight real-world datasets demonstrates that MA-Memento achieves an average improvement of 23.57% over fine-tuning approaches, with statistically significant results including 17.89% improvement in credit risk assessment (p < 0.001) and consistent superior performance across high-frequency trading, fraud detection, and AI benchmark scenarios. The framework successfully handles datasets ranging from 2,000 to 250,000 records, demonstrating scalability and practical applicability. Our coordinated multi-agent memory system enables real-time adaptation with formal theoretical guarantees, addressing critical gaps in existing approaches for mission-critical financial deployments. We provide rigorous mathematical proofs establishing convergence properties and comprehensive experimental validation using 64.14 MB of realistic financial and benchmark datasets."}]", "excerpt_truncated": true, "source_sha256": "202baf76d80c509d2f64fb338f9b8b239d519887c5db08b2901476b29d9fb2cb", "verification_required": true, "topic_domain": "judgment_and_consensus", "evidence_role": "discovery", "host_tier": "discovery", "source_identity": null, "persistent_identifiers": ["doi:10.18653/v1/2025.emnlp-main.1562", "doi:10.36227/techrxiv.175760292.25429267/v1", "openalex:W4416035436"], "source_candidates": ["https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2025.emnlp-main.1562", "https://aclanthology.org/2025.emnlp-main.1562.pdf", "https://doi.org/10.36227/techrxiv.175760292.25429267/v1"], "source_candidate_identities": {}}

